+	// VGS CHANGE: Epic makes each splat's colour linear here and blends in linear light,
+	// which BlendInSRGB 0 still does.
+	// Captures are trained blending sRGB values, and the VGS viewer draws them that way, so
+	// the colour stays sRGB, clamped to [0, 1] as the viewer clamps it, and the blended
+	// result is made linear in VGSSplatInverseToneCurvePostBlend.usf. Blending in linear
+	// light makes faint splats show far more than they were trained to (a 20 % splat over
+	// black gives 48 % of its colour instead of 20 %): coloured haze around hair and edges.
+	if (BlendInSRGB != 0u)
+	{
+		Color = saturate(Color + 0.5f);
+	}
+	else
